From 5ee621efbca66256ea53d05c35b43d6144523973 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:53:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/26] B70-QSA-04: Qwen4Exp QSA attention on XPU: fused
 prepare, portable unfused path

- use_fused_qk_norm_rope_gate accepts XPU, as Qwen3NextAttention already does
  (the same Triton fused_qk_rmsnorm_rope_gate); with the 128/64 indexer shape
  this also enables the fused qsa_prepare launch (indexer norm/RoPE/ring store/
  compression + main QK-norm/RoPE/gate + main K/V write) on XPU.
- B70_QSA_FUSED_PREPARE=0 forces the unfused kernels (A/B, fallback).
- Unfused path off CUDA: gemma_rmsnorm via the GemmaRMSNorm module instead of
  flashinfer, RoPE via forward_native instead of forward_cuda (vllm_flash_attn).
- QSAIndexer._metadata ran a host torch.equal whenever positions were not
  is_cuda, which includes XPU: a sync inside graph capture. Now CPU-only.
- One-time log line with the chosen paths.
---
 vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/indexer_qsa.py | 34 +++++++++++++++++----
 vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/qsa.py         | 19 +++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 46 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

